{
  "schema": "laya-executor-control-transport-rtl-input-v1",
  "scope": "Finite RTL control bridge with actual original handoff shell and depth2 512-bit request, request-echo and response FIFOs. Full 16-beat request collection precedes the shell's actual 8192-bit consumer handshake; only that handshake emits the original 16-beat echo. Real response FIFO writes and actual pops are counted separately; neither last write nor last pop acknowledges the shell. An independent 8192-bit accepted record must match the retained stable full response after all 16 writes and reads before accepted-lane full_n allows its actual write to acknowledge the shell. Early/foreign/replayed accepted attempts have full_n=0, no actual fire and no receipt count increment; only the separate rejection lane actually consumes and counts bounded notifications without release. Tail2/tail1 waits12, blocked early/foreign/replayed accepted attempts, matching rejection, cancellation in a partial request, immutable GRANT with pending ABORT, and persistent cancel old-response/cleanup progress. Exact accepted CLOSED receipt also supplies the original managed shell's complete closed-consumer record once. Offline actual C++ helper control stimuli and independent literal response gold are frozen from a verified helper-only host attempt. The executor-side full consumer is a TB byte-oracle peer, not generated executor RTL. Predecessor/safety/protection, query bytes/consumer pulses, terminal work and Host facts are controlled. Reset separates diagnostic cases; no reset is used to clear an active canceled half-frame or presented response. No same-runtime HLS executor/helper, real hub/monitor/LPV/AXI, production source protection, actual request retirement, physical safe closure/rearm, full model/graph, arithmetic, OOC, resources, timing or board claim.",
